Description: On-screen settings menu (cog) with power off and restart
 On the XDJ400 the touchscreen is the only input device: there is no
 keyboard, no mouse and no desktop shell behind Mixxx. Shutting the unit
 down cleanly meant sshing in, and hold-to-restart (holding a LOAD button
 for 7s) is a recovery gesture, not something you would explain to anyone
 else using the deck.
 .
 This adds the controls behind a settings panel the skin opens from a cog
 in the topbar. POWER OFF and RESTART are tap-again-to-confirm: the first
 press sets arm_power / arm_restart, which the skin uses to swap the
 button for a red "TAP AGAIN TO ..." face; the second press commits.
 Arming one option disarms the other, BACK and the cog press menu_disarm,
 and a 5s timer disarms both -- a menu left open mid-set never leaves a
 live one-tap kill on screen.
 .
 Restart reuses triggerRestart() from the hold-to-restart patch, so both
 routes share one implementation. Power off runs "systemctl poweroff",
 falling back to passwordless sudo (the same mechanism the USB eject
 already uses) for setups where logind/polkit will not grant the session
 the right; if every route is refused a POWER OFF FAILED banner says so
 instead of leaving the operator tapping a dead button.
 .
 Playback is deliberately untouched by opening the menu -- the panel is a
 skin overlay, so a set keeps running while it is open.
